# The dbt job's own dependency set (pipeline/DBT.md's CI plan), compiled to
# requirements-dbt.txt with pip-compile on Python 3.12 - the version that job
# pins (pipeline-tests.yml's `dbt` job says why it still does). Separate from
# requirements.in on purpose: the pytest job never needs dbt, and the dbt job
# never needs rasterio/pillow/pmtiles.
#
# duckdb is pinned identically to requirements.in's hand-written pin, and for
# the same ABI reason - the spatial extension is ABI-locked to the exact
# DuckDB version. Keep the two pins moving together. In this file it serves
# load_raw.py, which writes the fixture warehouse; dbt itself no longer
# imports it (next paragraph).
duckdb==1.5.5
#
# dbt v2, the Apache-2.0 distribution (#1793 - Rebuild the data platform as
# dlt -> dbt: seven contracted marts, a monthly refresh, published docs, and
# lighter phone downloads; the maintainer chose dbt-oss 2.0.5 over dbt 2.0.6,
# whose PyPI page carries no licence). One version everywhere, no dbt-core
# 1.x beside it. v2 is a Rust binary with its own DuckDB driver built in, so
# dbt-duckdb leaves, and so does sqlfluff-templater-dbt, which needs dbt-core.
#
# HOW IT INSTALLS, read from PyPI 2026-10-01, because it is not a wheel: PyPI
# holds one 5,062-byte sdist for 2.0.5 whose build backend
# (`_dbt_sa_build`) downloads the prebuilt wheel for this platform from
# github.com/dbt-labs/dbt/releases/download/v2.0.5 and refuses it unless its
# sha256 matches the sdist's own `assets.json`. So an install reaches GitHub
# as well as PyPI. The wheels are cp311-abi3 (Linux x86-64 and ARM, macOS,
# Windows x86-64): any CPython >= 3.11, which is `Requires-Python`.
#
# The DuckDB v2 bundles is 1.5.4, not the 1.5.5 above. pipeline-tests.yml's
# `dbt` job says what is measured about that split and what is not.
dbt-oss==2.0.5
#
# SQLFluff with its own jinja templater (pipeline/.sqlfluff). 4.3.0 is the
# newest release on PyPI, read 2026-10-01.
sqlfluff==4.3.0
